  "ciryl-gane-josh-hokit": {
   "summary": "Hokit shot in the first seconds and then marched forward through Gane's jabs and uppercuts, slamming him late in round 1; Sherdog's scorers still gave Gane the round on the cleaner shots. Gane stopped kicking for fear of the takedown and spent his energy moving, and Hokit took rounds 2 and 3 with right hands, clinch elbows and foot stomps. Hokit had little left from round 4; Gane's knees, uppercuts and body work took the last two rounds, and he won 48-47 on all three cards, as all three Sherdog scorers had it.",
   "turning_point": "Round 4: Hokit's shots lost their steam and Gane took over in the clinch with knees and short uppercuts.",
